{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1788216258811,"sessionID":"ses_fa601b9d5ffegNaU40qlNZbt8H","part":{"id":"prt_059feb0f5001ulvYWWxsuhlKrC","messageID":"msg_059fead1a0016dEy0bNGpU0Q32","sessionID":"ses_fa601b9d5ffegNaU40qlNZbt8H","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1788216264799,"sessionID":"ses_fa601b9d5ffegNaU40qlNZbt8H","part":{"id":"prt_059febcf9001DTR0pIyqkQelP7","messageID":"msg_059fead1a0016dEy0bNGpU0Q32","sessionID":"ses_fa601b9d5ffegNaU40qlNZbt8H","type":"text","text":"I found the root causes in the current implementation: it splits CSV lines manually, only accepts a single `--where`, treats `-created_at` as a literal field name, and derives headers from the first result row so empty selections can lose the requested columns. I’m patching those behaviors and adding regression tests around the missing-field and invalid-expression cases.","time":{"start":1788216261881,"end":1788216264788},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_032503d46c7d320f016a9603c5cb9c87d29fc31d43e7a34575","phase":"commentary"}}}}
